          "end": 8.16,
          "en": "which stands for Hypertext Transfer Protocol.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.16,
          "end": 9.69,
          "en": "Of course, we are not here to discuss about,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.69,
          "end": 10.77,
          "en": "what is a protocol?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 10.77,
          "end": 11.88,
          "en": "We are here to discuss,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 11.88,
          "end": 15.6,
          "en": "what are the methods which we can use to work with HTTP.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 15.6,
          "end": 16.5,
          "en": "See if you remember,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 16.5,
          "end": 19.08,
          "en": "when we were building this application for Job,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 19.08,
          "end": 22.23,
          "en": "we have used two methods: the GET and the POST.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 22.23,
          "end": 24.69,
          "en": "Now, when we want to fetch data from the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 24.69,
          "end": 26.55,
          "en": "we use something called a GET request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 26.55,
          "end": 29.82,
          "en": "So in the CRUD operations, if you want to read something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 29.82,
          "end": 31.26,
          "en": "we use the GET method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 31.26,
          "end": 33.48,
          "en": "But what if you want to create a resource?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 33.48,
          "end": 36.09,
          "en": "So you want to send some data from client to server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 36.09,
          "end": 37.2,
          "en": "which maybe you want to save",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 37.2,
          "end": 38.7,
          "en": "that in a database or something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 38.7,
          "end": 40.11,
          "en": "But if you want to send data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 40.11,
          "end": 43.41,
          "en": "if you want to create something on the server, we use POST.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 43.41,
          "end": 45.45,
          "en": "So POST is for sending data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 45.45,
          "end": 48.03,
          "en": "Now, we can also use it for updating data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 48.03,
          "end": 50.04,
          "en": "but mostly we use POST to create data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 50.04,
          "end": 51.99,
          "en": "But what if you want to update something?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 51.99,
          "end": 54.12,
          "en": "In that case, you can use PUT.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 54.12,
          "end": 56.19,
          "en": "So you can use PUT request for the updating.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 56.19,
          "end": 58.35,
          "en": "And then we have a DELETE as well, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 58.35,
          "end": 60.81,
          "en": "So in the HTTP, we also have a DELETE method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 60.81,
          "end": 62.97,
          "en": "So just like CRUD, we have DELETE-DELETE,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 62.97,
          "end": 65.07,
          "en": "so we have it the same for the HTTP.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 65.07,
          "end": 66.66,
          "en": "So in HTTP, we have different methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 66.66,
          "end": 71.66,
          "en": "The famous four is POST, GET, PUT, and DELETE.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 71.76,
          "end": 75,
          "en": "So if you want to use that in the Spring Boot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 75,
          "end": 77.52,
          "en": "we have talked about GetMapping and PostMapping.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 77.52,
          "end": 78.72,
          "en": "What about PUT?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 78.72,
          "end": 79.98,
          "en": "So we have PutMapping.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 79.98,
          "end": 81.48,
          "en": "What if you have DELETE?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 81.48,
          "end": 82.83,
          "en": "You have DeleteMapping.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 82.83,
          "end": 84.49,
          "en": "So now, let's say if we talk about the URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 84.49,
          "end": 87.06,
          "en": "which we talked about in the rest,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 87.06,
          "end": 89.22,
          "en": "if you want to add a new job,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 89.22,
          "end": 92.163,
          "en": "you will use your URL /job, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 94.02000000000001,
          "end": 94.85300000000001,
          "en": "That's for create.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 94.85300000000001,
          "end": 99.47999999999999,
          "en": "If you want to get a particular job, same URL /job.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 99.47999999999999,
          "end": 100.47,
          "en": "Both are same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 100.47,
          "end": 102.15,
          "en": "The difference is the methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 102.15,
          "end": 104.94,
          "en": "For the creation of the job, you will use POST.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 104.94,
          "end": 107.34,
          "en": "For the getting the job, you will use GET method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 107.34,
          "end": 108.173,
          "en": "Two different methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 108.173,
          "end": 109.22999999999999,
          "en": "So from the client side as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 109.22999999999999,
          "end": 111.12,
          "en": "you have to mention POST.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 111.12,
          "end": 113.03999999999999,
          "en": "On the server side also you have to mention POST.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 113.03999999999999,
          "end": 114.75,
          "en": "In the server, we will be using PostMapping.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 114.75,
          "end": 115.62,
          "en": "But the question arises,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 115.62,
          "end": 117.39,
          "en": "how we are going to use these methods?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 117.39,
          "end": 118.65,
          "en": "If we talk about your browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 118.65,
          "end": 120.51,
          "en": "in the browser, we do have GET.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 120.51,
          "end": 122.34,
          "en": "So by default, the URL when you use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 122.34,
          "end": 124.53,
          "en": "it will throw a GET request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 124.53,
          "end": 125.91,
          "en": "But what about the POST?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 125.91,
          "end": 128.46,
          "en": "To send the POST request, we have to create a Form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 128.46,
          "end": 130.32,
          "en": "But then what if you don't want to get a form?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 130.32,
          "end": 131.94,
          "en": "What if you want to test it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 131.94,
          "end": 134.28,
          "en": "So, browser will not be having that option, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 134.28,
          "end": 136.41,
          "en": "And that's why we have to look for a client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 136.41,
          "end": 138.81,
          "en": "And that's where this client can be a React application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 138.81,
          "end": 140.7,
          "en": "or this client can be your testing client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 140.7,
          "end": 142.2,
          "en": "let's say Postman.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 142.2,
          "end": 143.76,
          "en": "So we'll see, how do we use Postman,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
